Summary: Install placeholder AMD and NVIDIA DLLs in 64-bit prefixes, for D3DMetal and DXMT
Category: graphics
Kind: feature
Origin: crossover
  Version: 26.3.0
  CW-Hacks: 22435
  URL: https://media.codeweavers.com/pub/crossover/source/crossover-sources-26.3.0.tar.gz
  Note: CrossOver 26.3.0 CW HACK 22435, the wine.inf part (loader/wine.inf.in)
    Source: (sources/wine/loader/wine.inf.in)
Upstream: no
Why: Have wineboot put placeholder atidxx64.dll, nvapi64.dll and nvngx.dll in a
 64-bit prefix's system32. CX's comment says only "for D3DMetal". No builtin
 DLLs have those names, so setupapi writes generic placeholder DLLs; with one in
 system32, a DLL of that name on a renderer's DLL path (D3DMetal's three; DXMT
 ships nvapi64.dll and nvngx.dll) can be loaded, which Wine otherwise refuses
 outside prefix setup. D3DMetal 3.0 needs Wine 10.4's GSBASE model, so it is
 supported on 10.0 only: from Wine 10.5 (WineHQ 3a16aabb) GSBASE points at the
 TEB while PE code runs, and D3DMetal 3.0 crashes when a program creates a DXGI
 factory (measured on 11.22). The 11.x copy has DXMT's two only.
Programs: none known
Evidence: Sikarugir 10.0_8: its share/wine/wine.inf has these lines with this
 comment; it is the only difference in share/.
Port: 10.0: CX 25.1.1 lacks this; CX 26.3's lines added to 10.0's [FakeDllsWin64] unchanged.
Status: 10.0: 2026-11-26: header only (the 11.x copy is now separate). In build0

diff --git a/loader/wine.inf.in b/loader/wine.inf.in
index 9288b58..7c491f5 100644
--- a/loader/wine.inf.in
+++ b/loader/wine.inf.in
@@ -746,6 +746,10 @@ HKLM,SOFTWARE\Microsoft\VisualStudio\14.0\VC\Runtimes\x86,"Version",2,"14.51.362
 [FakeDllsWin64]
 10,twain_64,sane.ds
 10,twain_64,gphoto2.ds
+; CW HACK 22435: fake DLLs for D3DMetal
+11,,atidxx64.dll,*
+11,,nvapi64.dll,*
+11,,nvngx.dll,*
 
 ; Wow64-only fake dlls
 [FakeDllsWow64]
